From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:24:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pbd/test: accept two-digit float exponents on Windows

StringConvertTest expects float_to_string() to produce the three digit
exponent of the legacy msvcrt printf ("3.4028234663852886e+038") on
every Windows build. Binaries linked against the Universal CRT, or
built with mingw-w64's C99 printf (__USE_MINGW_ANSI_STDIO, the MSYS2
default), print the standard two digit form ("e+38"), so the test
fails there although both strings parse back to the same value (which
the test checks separately).

Accept either representation on Windows.
---
 libs/pbd/test/string_convert_test.cc | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/pbd/test/string_convert_test.cc b/libs/pbd/test/string_convert_test.cc
index b8a856d..a96a716 100644
--- a/libs/pbd/test/string_convert_test.cc
+++ b/libs/pbd/test/string_convert_test.cc
@@ -464,7 +464,8 @@ _test_float_conversion ()
 	string str;
 	CPPUNIT_ASSERT (float_to_string (numeric_limits<float>::max (), str));
 #ifdef PLATFORM_WINDOWS
-	CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL (MAX_FLOAT_WIN, str);
+	/* msvcrt prints a three digit exponent, the UCRT and mingw's C99 printf two */
+	CPPUNIT_ASSERT (str == MAX_FLOAT_WIN || str == MAX_FLOAT_STR);
 #else
 	CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL (MAX_FLOAT_STR, str);
 #endif
@@ -476,7 +477,8 @@ _test_float_conversion ()
 
 	CPPUNIT_ASSERT (float_to_string (numeric_limits<float>::min (), str));
 #ifdef PLATFORM_WINDOWS
-	CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL (MIN_FLOAT_WIN, str);
+	/* msvcrt prints a three digit exponent, the UCRT and mingw's C99 printf two */
+	CPPUNIT_ASSERT (str == MIN_FLOAT_WIN || str == MIN_FLOAT_STR);
 #else
 	CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL (MIN_FLOAT_STR, str);
 #endif
